{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14976","id":5196671316,"node_id":"PR_kwDODKw3uc8AAAABNb7pVA","html_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14976","diff_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14976.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14976.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/issues/14976","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14976/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/14976/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/issues/14976/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/statuses/6ceb78a575d98dbe06ac366e42501c67aee2b1c4","number":14976,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use a synthetic namespace for triage fixtures","user":{"login":"BagToad","id":47394200,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mzk0MjAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47394200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad","html_url":"https://github.com/BagToad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BagToad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},"body":"<!--\nThank you for contributing to GitHub CLI!\n\nIf you are proposing a fix for a security issue, STOP and follow .github/SECURITY.md instead.\n\nKeep the entire pull request self-contained, reviewer-facing, and diegetic: describe the\nchange, rationale, and evidence within the context of the repository and pull request. Do not\nnarrate how the pull request was produced or refer to private conversations, prior agent work,\nor other behind-the-scenes context. Omit those details unless they materially affect review;\nif they do, state the relevant fact and its significance directly.\n-->\n\n<!-- List related issues here. Use `fixes` or `closes` keywords to associate an issue number. -->\n\n### Description\n\n<!--\nWhat's the problem? How are we addressing it?\n\nWrite for a reviewer who has not worked in this part of the codebase. Give them the\nbackground they need before the problem makes sense, and avoid jargon.\n-->\n\nUse `example.invalid` as the owner of synthetic repositories so triage can publish their URLs without querying a nonexistent repo.\n\nThe publisher currently checks fixture URLs against the live API, which blocked [this triage run](https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/42312299651). This updates the publisher, fixture defaults, and reproduction instructions together.\n\n### How did you test this change?\n\n<!--\nReport only actions you actually performed and results you actually observed, using factual\nfirst-person language (for example, \"I ran...\" and \"I saw...\"). Do not present planned,\nhypothetical, inferred, or merely expected scenarios as testing.\n\nAutomated test results do not belong here. Passing unit tests, `go test ./...` output, and\ncoverage numbers tell a reviewer nothing they cannot see from CI, so do not paste them.\n\nIf you did not exercise the changed behavior, write `Not tested` and explain why.\n\nUse one or more of these, whichever communicates best:\n\n1. Screenshots or GIFs of the real command running. Preferred whenever the change is visible\n   in terminal output. If output changed, show it before and after.\n2. Given/When/Then scenarios, but only when you actually executed the steps. For example:\n   Given I was in a repo with no open pull requests\n   When I ran `gh pr list`\n   Then I saw \"no open pull requests in cli/cli\"\n3. A natural language walkthrough of what you did by hand, the states you covered, and what\n   you saw, including error and edge cases.\n\nIf you leave this empty, your pull request will very likely be closed.\n-->\n\nI replayed the saved triage payload locally against an in-memory API. The old publisher stopped at the visibility lookup. With the new fixture owner, the updated publisher created four reports and one comment in the fake API. The captured command and output stayed unchanged.\n\nI also tried private and unavailable references, plus fixture links with invalid paths. Each stopped before any write. Nothing was posted to GitHub during these checks, and I haven't rerun the workflow.\n\n### Key points\n\n<!--\nTradeoffs you accepted, alternatives you rejected, and anything a reviewer would otherwise have to guess at.\n-->\n\n- GitHub [account names cannot contain periods](https://docs.github.com/en/enterprise-cloud@latest/admin/managing-iam/iam-configuration-reference/username-considerations-for-external-authentication#about-username-normalization), so `example.invalid` cannot identify a real owner. The `github.com` host stays unchanged.\n- Only that exact owner is exempt. Real private or unavailable references still block publication, including links inside captured output.\n- Captured commands and output are not rewritten.\n\n### Notes for reviewers\n\n<!--\nWhere should review start, and what should be read next? Call out anything you are unsure about.\n\nLink related issues or prior discussion, with one sentence on why each matters.\n-->\n\nStart with the [publisher's visibility check](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/86ef059323d9d802959ca79d5db769d5d152114d/.github/scripts/issue-triage-report.cjs#L305-L331), then the [fixture defaults](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/86ef059323d9d802959ca79d5db769d5d152114d/script/ghmock/gqlscaffold.go#L13-L20) and [workflow instructions](https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/86ef059323d9d802959ca79d5db769d5d152114d/.github/workflows/issue-triage.md#L435-L451).\n\nThe failed run triaged [#9604](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/9604). This fixes publication, not the CODEOWNERS behavior reported there. A fresh triage run is needed to use the new fixture convention.\n\nAdditional local checks:\n\n- `node --test .github/scripts/issue-triage-report.test.cjs` - passed, 116 cases.\n- `GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.27.3 go -C script/ghmock fix ./...` - passed.\n- `GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.27.3 GOMAXPROCS=4 go -C script/ghmock test ./...` - passed.\n- `GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.27.3 GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./...` - passed.\n- `GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.27.1 GOMAXPROCS=4 make lint` - passed, no issues.\n- `gh aw compile issue-triage --shellcheck --no-check-update` - passed, no warnings.\n\n### Authorship and follow-up\n\n<!--\nREQUIRED - If you are an AI agent filling in this template, answer \"Who wrote this\" for yourself and answer honestly. For \"Who answers review comments,\" use only a choice the human has explicitly made in the conversation. If no choice has already been established, pause and ask the human to choose one of the three options before creating or updating the pull request. Do not infer the choice from repository ownership, authorship, assignees, prior interactions, or the current operator. After the human answers, check exactly the option they chose; the last option is valid when the human explicitly chooses nobody.\n\nCheck exactly one box in each list.\n-->\n\nWho wrote this:\n\n- [ ] A human wrote it.\n- [ ] An agent wrote it under close human direction.\n- [x] An agent wrote it independently, and no human has guided the implementation beyond the initial prompt.\n\nWho answers review comments:\n\n- [x] @BagToad will read and reply directly.\n- [ ] An agent will draft replies and @BagToad will read them before they are posted.\n- [ ] Nobody has explicitly committed to replying.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-07T00:19:18Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T01:48:49Z","closed_at":"2026-11-07T01:48:47Z","merged_at":"2026-11-07T01:48:47Z","merge_commit_sha":"736c68f674113337685e3eb1f908602a03b8f99b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"sergiou87","id":1083228,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODMyMjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1083228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87","html_url":"https://github.com/sergiou87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergiou87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":true},{"login":"babakks","id":36728931,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzI4OTMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36728931?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks","html_url":"https://github.com/babakks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babakks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baba